{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7649","id":5210682332,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNpSz3A","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7649","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7649.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7649.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7649","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7649/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7649/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7649/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/77ea206fb58119d4ff3f8fd97a6ae6f9df093a98","number":7649,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"doc(atlas): decision — one embedding model for every tier (#6060)","user":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #6060.\n\n## Decision\n\n**One embedding model for every Atlas tier** — cross-tier comparability by construction, not by correction at merge time. The per-tier-models + normalization route (per-model calibration, rank-based merge, per-tier quotas) is considered and rejected in the record, with reasons.\n\nThe record is grounded in the current code:\n\n- `merge_top_k` (`pkgs/atlas-search/crates/atlas-core/src/shards/scan.rs`) sorts raw cosine distance across all scanned shards — meaningful only in one vector space.\n- `atlas_manifest` records `metric` (validated: cosine only) but **no embedding model** — the one-model invariant that exists today in practice (`atlas-embed`: `snowflake-arctic-embed-m-v2.0`, local ONNX, 768d) is unenforced and unobservable.\n- The mandated model already runs locally, so the secret tier's local/API split is about where the same weights execute, not which model: no secret text needs an external embedding API.\n\n## Contract (M1–M6)\n\n- **M1/M2:** one model identity per fan-out; `atlas_manifest` gains an `embedding_model` key, validated at fan-out like the metric check — mixed-model sets fail loud, never merge partially.\n- **M3:** merge stays exact raw-distance; no per-tier score transforms at merge/rescore.\n- **M4:** tier boundary untouched — ceiling filtering still happens before merge; comparability never admits a shard (#6021/#5755 unaffected).\n- **M5:** query trace (#6027) records `embedding_model` per candidate and `query_embedding_model` at the head; a mixed-model trace is evidence of a breach, filed as a defect.\n- **M6:** embed pipeline and staging promotion assert the mandated model.\n\nCost consequences are stated in the record: a model change is a full-corpus re-embed with atomic cutover; tiers cannot adopt models independently; a tier that cannot run the mandated model stays out of cross-tier fan-out rather than diverging silently.\n\n## Implementation follow-ons (filed)\n\n- #7646 — manifest `embedding_model` key + fan-out validation (M1/M2)\n- #7647 — query-trace per-candidate model provenance (M5)\n- #7648 — embed pipeline / staging promotion assertion (M6)\n\nDocs only; no code, tests, or behaviour change in this PR.\n\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=repo-worker-code lane=code-h task=13030 -->\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796726908&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7649&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7649&signature=84c7b965dda9e2883e2a88cd4488b28621d2921747559887ad901967e0df4392\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7649?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:48:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T11:15:19Z","closed_at":"2026-11-08T11:15:16Z","merged_at":"2026-11-08T11:15:16Z","merge_commit_sha":"68480ba1f57dd11fb043db1ec162322f5f665df0","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.co